Original metadata provider, cmap/UVS, font/glyph metrics and AVAR algorithms are
compiled unchanged in Rust/WASM. No mature parser/shaper algorithm was ported
to TypeScript. The own original shaper adapter is pinned byte-for-byte and
extended by local typed data transport, not a parallel runtime/registry.

Original Unicode16 contextual itemizer, Clipper2/BSL-1.0, Earcut/ISC and Native
owner/shaders/Glow/Layer retain existing licences and source evidence.
Four actual Noto fixtures retain original fixed identities/OFL1.1 licences.
No Adobe source/assets are imported.

FontTools4.68.0/MIT is an independent TEST-ONLY reference, already installed in
the own isolated shaping Python environment. Preserve its original wheel
identity and prior notices; it is not added to runtime/package dependencies.
No new model/font downloads, root npm dependencies, locks, SDK pins or
WASM permissions were changed. Main owns formal R1 identity/exports/L3.

Post-layout adjustments use small independent CPU Float64 affine/spacing
calculations over canonical TextLayoutData. Pulling in another editor's
document/timeline/renderer or a complete paragraph model would cost more than
these adapters. Actual pixels are produced exclusively by existing admitted
Native GPU F16/F32; no CPU/Canvas8/browser fallback or new GPU owner is created.
